---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About GrooveMap"
  description="Learn how GrooveMap connects open music catalog data into a navigable knowledge graph."
  path="/about/"
>
  <article class="article shell">
    <header class="article-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">About GrooveMap</p>
      <h1>Music discovery starts between the rows.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Catalogs tell us what exists. GrooveMap is being built to reveal how
        those releases, people, labels, and creative histories connect.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="article-grid">
      <section aria-labelledby="mission-heading">
        <h2 id="mission-heading">The mission</h2>
        <p>
          GrooveMap combines structured music data from Discogs and MusicBrainz
          into graph and analytical models. The goal is a transparent foundation
          for exploration, recommendations, catalog research, and questions that
          are difficult to answer one release at a time.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="method-heading">
        <h2 id="method-heading">The method</h2>
        <p>
          Dedicated ingestion and enrichment services preserve source context
          while building explicit contracts between catalog data, graph
          relationships, analytical tables, APIs, and public experiences.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="principles-heading">
        <h2 id="principles-heading">The principles</h2>
        <ul class="principles">
          <li>
            <strong>Traceable:</strong> keep provenance and source identities
            visible.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Composable:</strong> publish clear interfaces instead of
            hidden monorepo coupling.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Respectful:</strong> treat access, licensing, and privacy as
            real architecture boundaries.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Useful:</strong> turn catalog structure into routes for
            genuine discovery.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>

    <aside class="callout" aria-labelledby="status-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Project structure</p>
        <h2 id="status-heading">Focused repositories, shared contracts</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        GrooveMap separates ingestion, persistence, graph enrichment, analytics,
        APIs, exploration, design, deployment, and operator tooling into public
        repositories with explicit ownership boundaries.
      </p>
    </aside>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
